I was playing a lawful Samurai, and while in a temple of my own god, I 
accidentally attacked the priest of the temple.  Because the priest was now
angry with no way to pacify him, I was forced to fight for my life, so I zapped
him with a polymorph wand and killed him.  I assumed my god would be upset 
about this, so I killed another monster and sacrificed the corpse.  However, my
sacrifice was accepted with no message about him being angry, so I decided to
pray.  He was not angry when I prayed either, and even gave me a spellbook of
healing, so I assumed everything was OK.

The only thing that bothers me now is that when I enter the temple now, I get
the message "You have a forbidding feeling."  I thought this may have been
because I changed alignment but was still sacrificing to my old god, thereby
allowing the sacrifices to work.  Is there any cause for worry?  Can I continue
as before with my god?  Am I aggravating monsters now?

On a last note, to prevent such mistakes in the future, I think it would be
nice to have three settings for dealing with peaceful monsters:  attack without
confirmation, confirm before attacking, and a "safe" setting like with your pet
so that it is impossible to attack peaceful monsters ("You stop to avoid
hitting someone you will regret attacking for the rest of the game.")  This
would also eliminate an extra keystroke by not needing a confirmation about
whether to attack or not.  Does this sound like a good idea?
